            "findings": [
              {
                "id": "R1-001",
                "lens": "risk",
                "location": "engine/projection/evidencelog/log.go:78-115",
                "severity": "SUGGESTION",
                "claim": "The sidecar append is guarded: identifiers are validated, directories are created via statestore.EnsureDirs, the final component is opened with O_NOFOLLOW, and the file is created at 0600 under a lock. A pre-planted FIFO is not blocked on because of O_NONBLOCK, though O_WRONLY on a FIFO with no reader fails with ENXIO and surfaces as an error. No reachable exploit was found. The sidecar stores only the response hash and byte count, not the response body, so no data exposure was found.",
                "proof_refs": [
                  "engine/projection/evidencelog/log.go:78-115",
                  "engine/statestore/statestore_unix.go:23-28"
                ]
              }
            ],
            "evidence": [
              "Reviewed all 21 manifest paths. Most are golden and test updates for the new PostToolUse projection family entries.",
              "Uninstall (engine/settings/merge.go) now also scans PostToolUse, and ownership is still checked by entry shape, so foreign PostToolUse entries are preserved. The updated test covers this.",
              "The new evidencelog adapter enforces symlink refusal, 0600/0700 permissions, identifier validation (rejecting path traversal), and a lock. The test covers symlink and unsafe-ID refusal.",
              "No secrets, new dependencies, or unsafe input handling were introduced."
            ]
