            "lens": "review-resilience",
            "findings": [],
            "evidence": [
              "evidencelog.Append takes a per-workflow lock with a bounded wait and returns a wrapped error if it fails. It writes one O_APPEND line and joins the write, sync and close errors, so a failed append is reported to the caller and never silently dropped.",
              "The sidecar is opened with O_NOFOLLOW and O_NONBLOCK. A symlink is refused with a specific error, and a FIFO with no reader fails instead of blocking, so a bad sidecar cannot hang the hook.",
              "Append-only writes under a lock keep the cost of a read independent of file size. The per-append fsync adds latency, but this diff shows no measured impact and no code path that calls it, so I report no finding.",
              "The new PostToolUse projection entries are added after the existing entries, so an older install is completed by the next merge without disturbing existing entries. removeHooks now also scans PostToolUse, so uninstall removes the new entries. The tests cover both.",
              "Status now reports an older install as missing the PostToolUse parts until the user reinstalls the hooks. This follows from the requested change, and the golden files were updated to match."
            ]
          }
        }
      },
